## Optionally add InfiniBand support services on *head node*

The following command adds OFED and PSM support using base distro-provided
drivers to the chosen *head node*.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Optionally add InfiniBand support services on head node -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ib -->
```bash
{{ pkg_group_install }} "InfiniBand Support"
# Load IB services
udevadm trigger --type=devices --action=add
systemctl restart rdma-load-modules@infiniband.service
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->

{% include 'network/infiniband/opensm.md.j2' %}

With the InfiniBand drivers included, you can also enable (optional) IPoIB
functionality which provides a mechanism to send IP packets over the IB network.
If you plan to mount a Lustre file system over InfiniBand, then having IPoIB
enabled is a requirement for the Lustre client. The following creates a
NetworkManager connection for the IPoIB interface `${ipoib_dev}` on the *head
node*, with the address `${sms_ipoib}` and subnet prefix
`${ipoib_prefix_length}`. Set `${ipoib_dev}` to the name the system gives the
interface, for example `ibp3s0` under predictable interface naming, and add one
connection per port if the system contains dual-ported or multiple HCAs.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Optionally enable IPoIB interface on head node -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_ipoib -->
```bash
# Define the local IPoIB interface, address, and subnet prefix
nmcli connection add type infiniband con-name ipoib ifname "${ipoib_dev}" \
	ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses "${sms_ipoib}/${ipoib_prefix_length}"

# Bring up the IPoIB interface
nmcli connection up ipoib
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
